<title>USA: Horizon Cellular extends tender offer.</title>
<headline>Horizon Cellular extends tender offer.</headline>
<dateline>MALVERN, Pa. 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Horizon Cellular Telephone Co and Horizon Finance Corp said on Friday that the offer to buy and solicitation of consents for their 11-3/8 percent senior subordinated discount notes due 2000 had been extended.</p>
<p>The company said in a statement the offer had been extended to 5 p.m. EDT on Sept 27. It was scheduled to expire at 5 p.m. EDT on Friday.</p>
<p>At the close of business on Friday, tenders and consent for about $41.9 million in notes had been received, the statement said.</p>
<p>Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette is dealer manager.</p>
<p>-- New York newsroom, (212) 859-1610</p>
